# Knowledge Assets

Files in `docs/` are governed Knowledge Assets: containers for meaning, not casual notes. Use `templates/knowledge-assets/KNOWLEDGE_ASSET_TEMPLATE.md` as a starter structure; templates are drafts, not governed assets.

For capture routing and promotion discipline, see `docs/operations/OPM-002_KNOWLEDGE_CAPTURE_WORKFLOW.md` (Approved / Advisory). Do not over-promote observations into formal assets.

For decision promotion and approval, see `docs/operations/OPM-003_DECISION_PROMOTION_APPROVAL_WORKFLOW.md` (Approved / Advisory).

## Placement

Place new assets in the appropriate `docs/` subfolder per `docs/README.md`.

## Required metadata

Add or update metadata when creating or substantially revising formal assets. Use the current Knowledge Asset standard rather than copying stale examples.

Every formal asset should identify, as applicable:

- stable Knowledge Asset ID;
- title;
- classification and category;
- status and Authority Level;
- Canonical Source designation;
- human owner;
- Primary AI Owner or stewardship role, if any;
- creation and last-updated dates;
- review cadence;
- related assets;
- AI Consumption;
- Change Impact.

## Every asset must answer

- Why it matters
- Who owns it
- Whether it is authoritative
- What decisions it informs
- What context would be lost without it
- How future agents should use it

## Status and promotion

- Do not set Approved, Canonical, or Governing without explicit Founder approval.
- Eunomia may assess, recommend, draft, initiate authorized low-risk maintenance, and route stewardship work under GDR-004, but may not approve.
- Eunomia is a defined ecosystem role, not yet an active agent or application component.
- Backlog questions are not decisions; lessons and research notes are evidence, not decisions.
- Proposed is not Approved; do not use Exploratory status on Decision Records.
- When superseding an asset, update its status and link the replacement.
- Keep exploratory content clearly labeled until promoted.
- Any maintenance performed under Eunomia stewardship must report what changed, why, the supporting evidence or authority, the impact, the next owner, and unresolved issues.

For ID prefixes, status models, authority hierarchy, and stewardship boundaries, see GDR-001, OLY-GOV-002, OLY-GOV-003, and GDR-004.
